1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,760
Next tool, metal fab laser, welder, 1200 watt unboxing and first use.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,840
Take out all the items.

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:10,240
Pay attention to the unboxing tips.

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,240
Open the lid first.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:46,400
Pull apart from the side to open and remove the enclosure.

6
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:55,890
Take out the welding head first, then remove the foam.

7
00:00:55,890 --> 00:01:25,460
Wind the cable on the side of the main unit, and place the welding head on the bracket.

8
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,980
Place the main unit.

9
00:01:27,980 --> 00:01:32,860
Leave a gap of more than 10 centimeters at the front and back of the main unit.

10
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:41,930
Lock the four caster wheels.

11
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:52,040
Connect the shielding gas cylinder.

12
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:59,110
Insert one end of the tube into the shielding gas inlet on the main unit.

13
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:03,470
Connect the other end of the tube to the cylinder, or gas generator.

14
00:02:03,470 --> 00:02:11,050
Place the welding head.

15
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:32,010
Assemble the welding head cradle.

16
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:34,130
Place the welding head on the cradle.

17
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:41,900
Connect the workpiece sensing cable.

18
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:45,860
Put the connector end into the port for the workpiece sensing cable.

19
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:50,140
Connect to a power supply.

20
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:56,460
This product requires a 220 to 240 volt AC power supply, and works at a rated power of

21
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:01,220
4.2 kilowatts and a full load current of 21 amperes.

22
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:06,500
An individual branch circuit with a current carrying capacity of 25 amperes or above is

23
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,500
recommended.

24
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:10,540
Ensure that the power supply is grounded.

25
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:13,780
The connection of power cables varies with their standards.

26
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:21,440
If hard wiring operation is required, it should be performed by a professional electrician.

27
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,840
Attach the round connector of the power cable to the main unit.

28
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:32,690
The larger pin faces upward.

29
00:03:32,690 --> 00:03:37,520
Check the emergency stop button.

30
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:41,480
Ensure that the emergency stop button is released.

31
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:45,460
Insert the key.

32
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:48,500
Insert the key into its designated port.

33
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:51,480
Power on and unlock the device.

34
00:03:51,480 --> 00:04:01,400
On the back panel of the main unit, turn on the power switch to activate the device.

35
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:06,260
On the touchscreen, select a language and unit.

36
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:10,660
The first time you turn on the device, you will see a QR code on the touchscreen.

37
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:15,860
Scan the QR code to watch the safety training videos.

38
00:04:15,860 --> 00:04:20,860
After watching the video, input the serial number shown on the touchscreen to the web.

39
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:23,980
To generate an unlock password for your device.

40
00:04:23,980 --> 00:04:27,740
On the touchscreen of your device, tap enter the password.

41
00:04:27,740 --> 00:04:32,140
Enter the password generated to unlock your device.

42
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,460
Calibrate the focus for the welding head.

43
00:04:34,460 --> 00:04:38,840
On the home page of the touchscreen, tap system settings and check the value of focus

44
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:43,190
scale reference.

45
00:04:43,190 --> 00:04:46,050
Check if the graduated tube is of the same value.

46
00:04:46,050 --> 00:04:48,470
If yes, no calibration is needed.

47
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:51,190
If not, adjust the graduated tube.

48
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:52,590
Open the fastener.

49
00:04:52,590 --> 00:04:56,630
Push or pull the graduated tube to adjust it to the reference value.

50
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,830
Connect the wire feeder.

51
00:04:58,830 --> 00:05:03,150
The wire feeder is used to feed wire in laser welding, and it is not needed in metal

52
00:05:03,150 --> 00:05:04,670
cleaning or cutting.

53
00:05:04,670 --> 00:05:07,790
Place the wire feeder on the left side of the main unit.

54
00:05:07,790 --> 00:05:10,630
Lock the four caster wheels.

55
00:05:10,630 --> 00:05:12,230
Connect to the main unit.

56
00:05:12,230 --> 00:05:15,190
Use the wire feeder cable to connect them.

57
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:20,240
The small protrusion on the inner wall faces upwards.

58
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,080
Insert the connector.

59
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:27,870
Screw the metal part.

60
00:05:27,870 --> 00:05:29,350
Install the drive rolls.

61
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:35,630
This video exemplifies installing 1mm welding wire on the 1mm guiding rail.

62
00:05:35,630 --> 00:05:38,350
Open the wire feeder.

63
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:42,350
Loosen the wire feeding driver.

64
00:05:42,350 --> 00:05:47,140
Remove the screws.

65
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:51,480
Install the drive rolls.

66
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:55,290
Install the screws back.

67
00:05:55,290 --> 00:06:04,670
Store the other pair of drive rolls above the wire feeding driver.

68
00:06:04,670 --> 00:06:07,310
Install the wire feeding tube.

69
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:10,070
Close the right tensioner.

70
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:14,310
Loosen the screw on the right side of the wire feeding driver.

71
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:18,390
Insert the end of the wire feeding tube without a fastener to the wire feeder.

72
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:22,310
Lead the nozzle in until its stem presses against the right panel of the wire feeding

73
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:23,670
driver.

74
00:06:23,670 --> 00:06:25,910
Tighten the screw to fix the nozzle.

75
00:06:25,910 --> 00:06:27,750
Open the right tensioner.

76
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:32,960
Load the welding wire.

77
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:38,260
Unscrew the cap and remove the sleeve.

78
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:46,840
Align the hole with the pin.

79
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:50,460
Ensure that the wire spool is installed in the correct direction.

80
00:06:50,460 --> 00:06:54,400
After released, the wire comes out from the bottom of the wire spool to enter the

81
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,360
wire feeding driver.

82
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:02,630
Install the sleeve and the cap back.

83
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,030
Take out the wire end.

84
00:07:04,030 --> 00:07:09,610
Do not release the wire or it will unravel.

85
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:13,570
Cut off the bent end of the wire.

86
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:18,820
Thread the wire into the wire feeding driver.

87
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:21,220
Press the wire slightly to make it pass through.

88
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:28,910
Ensure that the wire passes through the drive rolls into the wire feeding tube.

89
00:07:28,910 --> 00:07:32,410
Close the tensioners.

90
00:07:32,410 --> 00:07:41,660
Rotate the tensioner's knobs to adjust the wire feed tension.

91
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:45,700
Feed the welding wire.

92
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:52,020
When delivered, the wire feeding tube is installed with a 0.8 slash 1.0 nozzle at the end with

93
00:07:52,020 --> 00:07:55,710
a fastener.

94
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:58,150
Press and hold the feed button on the wire feeder.

95
00:07:58,150 --> 00:08:02,090
The wire spool rotates counterclockwise at a constant speed.

96
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:05,430
When the wire extends from the nozzle, stop wire feeding.

97
00:08:05,430 --> 00:08:11,230
If the wire extends too far, press the retract button to return the wire.

98
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:14,470
Close the door of the wire feeder.

99
00:08:14,470 --> 00:08:17,950
Install the wire feeding tube on the welding head.

100
00:08:17,950 --> 00:08:19,390
Open the fastener.

101
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:21,630
Slide it onto the welding head tip.

102
00:08:21,630 --> 00:08:25,650
Ensure that the wire comes out from the groove of the welding nozzle.

103
00:08:25,650 --> 00:08:31,540
Close the fastener.

104
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:36,790
Fine tune the wire.

105
00:08:36,790 --> 00:08:40,060
Secure the wire feeding tube.

106
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:42,620
Place back on the welding head cradle.

107
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:46,620
Use X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder 1200 watts.

108
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:51,780
Before operating the device, please follow the safety instructions to put on PPE and

109
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:54,500
take proper safety precautions.

110
00:08:54,500 --> 00:09:01,100
Necessary PPE includes laser safety goggles, welding helmets, dust mask, laser and heat-resistant

111
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:03,740
gloves, clothing, and aprons.

112
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:07,700
Ensure that the workroom is well ventilated.

113
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:10,320
Laser welding in standard mode.

114
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:16,340
Ensure that a gas flow meter is fitted to the gas cylinder, or gas generator.

115
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:20,320
Ensure that enable lasering is off.

116
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:24,070
Open the gas cylinder valve.

117
00:09:24,070 --> 00:09:28,270
Press and hold the grip sensing button and trigger to allow gas flow.

118
00:09:28,270 --> 00:09:35,140
Meanwhile, adjust the gas flow rate to 15 to 30 liters per minute.

119
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:38,260
Place the workpiece on a metal base.

120
00:09:38,300 --> 00:09:42,820
Put the workpiece sensing cable to the workpiece or to a conductive object connected with the

121
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:43,820
workpiece.

122
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:48,700
It is strictly prohibited to attach the clamp to the graduated tube of the welding head.

123
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:52,620
Press the feed and retract buttons on the welding head to adjust the wire until its

124
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:55,500
tip coincides with the red spot.

125
00:09:55,500 --> 00:09:58,780
Calibrate the welding head if the red spot falls at the left or right side of the

126
00:09:58,780 --> 00:10:02,900
extended wire, or if the spot is not visible or blurred.

127
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:07,260
Refer to the calibrate the red spot position part in maintenance.

128
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:11,980
Turn on the wire feeding enable switch to enable the auto feeding function.

129
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:15,700
On the touch screen, choose standard mode, weld.

130
00:10:15,700 --> 00:10:19,620
Select the material type, material thickness, and wire diameter.

131
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:22,820
Tap enable wire feeding to allow wire feeding.

132
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:25,980
And tap enable lasering to allow laser emission.

133
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,340
Align the parts to be welded.

134
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:31,780
Aiming the welding nozzle at the starting point, press and hold the grip sensing button

135
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,700
and trigger to start welding.

136
00:10:34,700 --> 00:10:38,780
Back weld the starting and ending points first, then start seam welding.

137
00:10:38,780 --> 00:10:42,900
As the welding head feeds the wire forward, a reaction force is generated from the

138
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:46,500
welding point that pushes the welding head backward.

139
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,940
Simply hold the welding head steady and guide the direction.

140
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:53,980
To avoid wire sticking, do not press the welding head downward.

141
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:57,500
After the welding is completed, the workpiece and parts of the welding head will

142
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,820
remain hot.

143
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:01,780
Do not touch the hot areas without protection.

144
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:05,540
Turn off enable wire feeding and enable lasering.

145
00:11:05,540 --> 00:11:07,820
Laser cleaning.

146
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:09,860
Turn off the device.

147
00:11:09,860 --> 00:11:14,520
Remove the wire feeding tube.

148
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:16,720
Remove the welding nozzle.

149
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:20,430
Replace with the cleaning nozzle.

150
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:22,670
Turn on the device.

151
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:23,750
Tap clean.

152
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:25,390
Tap enable lasering.

153
00:11:25,390 --> 00:11:26,390
Tap confirm.

154
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:30,350
Aim the cleaning nozzle at the starting point with the welding head parallel to the

155
00:11:30,350 --> 00:11:31,990
weld seam.

156
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:42,640
Press and hold the grip sensing button and trigger to start laser cleaning.

157
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:45,160
Laser cleaning is completed.

158
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,200
Laser cutting.

159
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:52,360
On the touch screen, tap system settings and take down the value of focus scale reference.

160
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,520
Turn off the device.

161
00:11:54,520 --> 00:12:00,210
Open the fastener to remove the current tip.

162
00:12:00,210 --> 00:12:03,420
Insert the cutting tip.

163
00:12:03,420 --> 00:12:06,460
Keep consistent with focus scale reference.

164
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,500
Close the fastener.

165
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:12,700
Place the gas flow meter on the cylinder with a gas pressure reducing valve.

166
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:17,780
Turn on the device and check if the welding head emits a clear and integral red spot.

167
00:12:17,780 --> 00:12:23,380
If not, calibrate the red spot position to avoid burning the nozzle during laser cutting.

168
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:31,210
Adjust the air pressure to 0.6 to 0.8 megapascals.

169
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:32,210
Tap cut.

170
00:12:32,210 --> 00:12:35,050
Select the material type and material thickness.

171
00:12:35,050 --> 00:12:36,610
Tap enable lasering.

172
00:12:36,610 --> 00:12:37,910
Tap confirm.

173
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:42,420
Start laser cutting.

174
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:44,260
Laser cutting is completed.

175
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,500
Replace the wire feeding nozzle.

176
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:50,660
The wire feeding tube has an end with a fastener and a replaceable nozzle.

177
00:12:50,660 --> 00:13:01,270
You need to replace the nozzle based on the diameter of the welding wire.

178
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:03,710
Clean or replace the lens protector.

179
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:08,350
If the laser power decreases and the welding spark weakens, the welding head's lens protector

180
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:10,790
may get dirty or damaged.

181
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:13,350
Clean or replace it as needed.

182
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:18,750
Please clean or replace the lens protector in a dust-free or relatively clean environment.

183
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:24,070
Before operations, clean the welding head with lint-free paper or lint-free cloth and

184
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:27,090
wash your hands or wear lint-free gloves.

185
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:30,930
Remove the cover on the top of the welding head.

186
00:13:30,930 --> 00:13:35,590
Remove the lens protector one.

187
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:37,110
Check the lens protector.

188
00:13:37,110 --> 00:13:41,670
If the lens protector is dirty, use a cotton swab dipped with alcohol to clean it.

189
00:13:41,670 --> 00:13:43,910
Then install it back to the welding head.

190
00:13:43,910 --> 00:13:49,470
If the lens protector is burned or heavily dirty and uncleanable, it needs to be replaced.

191
00:13:49,470 --> 00:13:58,940
Keep your hands clean or wear lint-free gloves to remove the gasket and lens protector.

192
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:02,410
Take out a new lens protector.

193
00:14:02,410 --> 00:14:07,810
Do not touch the glass with your fingers or other tools during replacement to prevent dirt.

194
00:14:07,810 --> 00:14:13,550
If the glass accidentally gets dirty or dusty, use a cotton swab to clean it.

195
00:14:13,550 --> 00:14:18,720
Remove the protective film on the top.

196
00:14:18,720 --> 00:14:21,520
Install the lens protector.

197
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:24,120
Remove the protective film on the other side.

198
00:14:24,120 --> 00:14:35,030
Install the gasket back.

199
00:14:35,030 --> 00:14:37,910
Install the lens protector back to the welding head.

200
00:14:37,910 --> 00:14:45,260
Install the lens protector in the correct direction and press it into place.

201
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:49,540
Calibrate the red spot position for the welding head.

202
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,460
Calibrate the left or right offset.

203
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:55,860
If you use the pre-installed welding nozzle for laser welding, perform a left or right

204
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:57,740
offset calibration.

205
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:03,540
When the laser spot deviates left or right from the wire, despite proper nozzle installation.

206
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:09,460
On the touchscreen of the main unit, tap system settings, machine settings, enter administrator

207
00:15:09,460 --> 00:15:11,220
settings.

208
00:15:11,220 --> 00:15:19,460
Then input the 8 digit password, 8888888.

209
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:22,960
To the right of red spot position offset, tap start.

210
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:27,420
Then tap the left arrow to decrease the offset and move the red spot leftward.

211
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:31,960
Tap the right arrow to increase the offset and move the red spot rightward.

212
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:36,400
When the center of the red spot falls at the welding wire, tap completed.

213
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:38,380
Calibrate the up or down offset.

214
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:43,180
When a cutting nozzle is used, the laser beam may strike the nozzle's inner wall, resulting

215
00:15:43,180 --> 00:15:48,200
in either blockage or reflection.

216
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:54,980
In such cases, perform left or right offset calibration.

217
00:15:54,980 --> 00:16:00,300
If the problem persists, reset the red spot position offset to zero and try calibrating

218
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:02,620
the up or down offset.

219
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:06,540
Welding and cleaning nozzles have larger apertures and typically do not require such

220
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,980
adjustment.

221
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:12,460
Insert the hex key into hole one or hole two and slowly turn the screw while observing

222
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:14,660
the light emitting from the nozzle.

223
00:16:14,660 --> 00:16:21,890
If a clear red spot appears, stop turning the screw.

224
00:16:21,890 --> 00:16:24,770
Replace the welding wire.

225
00:16:24,770 --> 00:16:30,310
Now we replace the 1 millimeter welding wire with a 1.2 millimeter welding wire.

226
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:35,690
Open the door of the wire feeder, unscrew the cap and remove the sleeve.

227
00:16:35,690 --> 00:16:38,770
Open the two tensioners.

228
00:16:38,770 --> 00:16:44,740
Rotate the wire spool clockwise to remove the wire from the wire feeding driver.

229
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:52,800
Take out the wire spool, bend the wire end and store it in the hole of the wire spool.

230
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:55,760
Remove the screws.

231
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:58,000
Remove the current drive rolls.

232
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,560
Remove the screws above the wire feeding driver.

233
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:04,560
Take out the drive roll stored above the wire feeding driver.

234
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:10,120
Be sure that the size on the outer side of the drive rolls matches the welding wires diameter.

235
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:13,580
Install the new pair of drive rolls.

236
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:16,240
Install the screws back.

237
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:21,040
Store the other pair of drive rolls above the wire feeding driver.

238
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:31,340
Replace the 0.8 slash 1.0 nozzle with the provided 1.2 slash 1.6 wire feeding nozzle.

239
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:34,360
Install the new wire spool.

240
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:35,820
Install the sleeve back.

241
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:39,140
Install the cap back.

242
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:41,380
Take out the wire end.

243
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:44,100
Cut off the bent end of the wire.

244
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:47,580
Thread the wire into the wire feeding driver.

245
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:52,180
Press the wire slightly to make it pass through.

246
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:58,080
Close the tensioners.

247
00:17:58,080 --> 00:18:03,970
Rotate the tensioners knobs to adjust the wire feed tension.

248
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:08,170
Press and hold the feed button on the wire feeder until the wire extends out from the

249
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:08,650
nozzle.
